VOnce a completed GNCSim architecture has been put together, and the Gimbaled TVC rocket is ready to simulate, a variety of unsafe conditions should be simulated via Monte Carlo (Rocket Angle from Vertical, Angular rates in Pitch, Yaw, and Roll). For each of these factors, a maximum safe condition shall be decided, based on whether the rocket can recover from the condition by the end of the burn of the motor. Because the values are a small change in software, this can be resolved later on in the design cycle. Additionally, GNCSim should simulate what happens after controls shutoff. GNCSim should consider cases of return back to 0, return back to 0 and cut power, just cutting power, etc...
